SDP.Item.Skill.healing.Description:
The Healing Skill represents your ability to treat wounds, combat illness, and stabilize people in danger.

A successful Healing Test notably allows you to:
Diagnose a wound, infection, or disease;
Treat a disease or limit its effects;
Restore a number of Wounds equal to your Intelligence Bonus + SL (a character may benefit from only one Healing Test per day);
Stop a hemorrhage (reduces Bleeding by 1 per SL achieved).

When bandages, poultices, or appropriate equipment are used, the GM may consider that the risk of infection is reduced or eliminated.

If you tend to someone affected by a disease, a successful Healing Test protects you from that disease for the day.

Some serious injuries require the Surgery Talent to be treated properly. The GM may apply bonuses or penalties depending on the severity of the wound, the quality of available equipment, or the conditions under which care is provided.

SDP.Item.Skill.animalcare.Description:
The Animal Care Skill represents your knowledge of domestic and wild creatures, as well as your ability to heal, understand, and look after them.

Possessing this Skill allows you to keep animals in good health under normal conditions without needing to make a Test. When a problem arises, an Animal Care Test may be used to identify its cause or provide appropriate care.

This Skill may notably be used to:
Detect a disease or injury;
Understand the cause of unusual behavior, disobedience, or discomfort;
Identify an animal's particular traits, needs, or characteristics;
Heal a number of Wounds equal to your Intelligence Bonus + SL (an animal may benefit from only one healing Test after each encounter);
Stop a Bleeding condition;
Prepare an animal for a performance, demonstration, or any other special activity.
